</section>

<section class="faq" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">Good To Know</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <div class="rule"></div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details open>
        <summary>Who do you work with?</summary>
        <p>I work with business owners who want to improve how their systems and technology support the way they work. You don't need a technical background or a particular type of business to get started.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do I need to know which service I want?</summary>
        <p>No. Book an introductory call and we'll work out which option makes sense for what you're trying to achieve.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What's the difference between a Working Session and a Systems Review?</summary>
        <p>A Working Session is for tackling a specific, defined issue together. A Systems Review is a more detailed assessment of how part of your business operates, followed by written recommendations and an action plan.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can you implement the recommendations?</summary>
        <p>Where the work is within my scope, yes. Implementation is quoted separately so you can decide whether you'd like help putting the recommendations into practice.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do I need to buy new software?</summary>
        <p>Not necessarily. Often the best starting point is making better use of what you already have.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can you help if I'm considering an app or new platform?</summary>
        <p>Yes. We can assess your requirements, compare options and look at feasibility and ongoing costs before you commit to development.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do you work remotely or in person?</summary>
        <p>Both, depending on the service and location. We'll agree on the most suitable format before booking.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is the introductory call free?</summary>
        <p>Yes. It's a free 20-minute conversation to understand what you need and establish whether I can help. Detailed consultancy, research and technical work take place through paid services.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

